From 0f3fcc932279bd9ceeceef373458e51330d39887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:48:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0294 -- CPU witness + SDL/0124 hardware
 witnesses at boot/emit

Nothing in any log witnessed which CPU ran a benchmark cell. Video is provable
from evidence and sound from is_sb16/dsp_ver/highdma, but the CPU was identified
ONLY by a digit the operator typed into a sweep BAT, which merely set the log-tag
prefix. Every cross-CPU conclusion in the campaign rested on that one keystroke.

Attest it in-engine at boot. Emit both identities: CPUID vendor + family/model/
stepping is exact, free, and separates Pentium (GenuineIntel family 5) from
Am5x86 (AuthenticAMD family 4) from Intel 486; then a MHz estimate mirrored from
setup/profile.c estimate_mhz() -- TSC-exact on Pentium, calibrated busy-loop on
486 with MHZ_486_LOOP_DIV=16400 UNCHANGED so engine numbers match SETUP's --
splits DX2-66 from DX2-50. CPUID absence falls back to the timing loop. cpu_class
buckets mirror profile.c detect_cpu(). Runs once at main() entry after
Logger::init, before SDL_Init and any flip, so the ~220 ms window is invisible to
fps. Default-ON, strict killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CPU_WITNESS=0.

Also folds the SDL-probe hardware witnesses into the manifest via SDL/0124 so
analysis stops grepping <TAG>SDL.LOG: video_vram_kb + video_lfb_or_banked (the
resolved flush path, which the 0019 Cirrus guard forces banked -- what the 1.2 fps
Cirrus deficit tracks), and audio_is_sb16 (identity = DSP major >= 4; SDL/0124 has
no IsSB16 by design), audio_dsp_ver, audio_dma_path, audio_force_8bit,
audio_dma_channel. Identity, override and outcome are SEPARATE fields so the X8
cell (a genuine SB16 forced to 8-bit to decouple card from DMA path) records
is_sb16=1 force_8bit=1 dma_path=8bit-low instead of self-obscuring. These getters
read persistent probe statics, so they are valid at emit even post SDL_Quit
(unlike the live timebase query in 0293). Plus the in-lane audio_backend + locked
logical video mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
